claude: true
prompt: |
  Drain the Net-Async-Crawl4AI karr board. This is the async IO::Async Crawl4AI
  client — an IO::Async::Notifier subclass wrapping WWW::Crawl4AI, returning
  Futures throughout (the same visible strategy chain, run non-blocking). Delegate
  behavior-relevant code to the net-async-crawl4ai-worker agent, tests to
  net-async-crawl4ai-test-writer, and release audits to
  net-async-crawl4ai-release-checker; follow
  .claude/rules/net-async-crawl4ai-rules.md. Never release. Reuse the sync building
  blocks from WWW::Crawl4AI — never fork them; work that belongs to the sister
  WWW::Crawl4AI is a ticket on that repo's board, not a local edit.
